Example: a midyear partial sale separates profit from money withdrawn.
Salary funds two FUND units bought on 2022-12-31 at 100 USD each, giving the report
an opening value of 200 USD on 2023-01-01. On 2023-07-01, one unit is sold
for 130 USD (@ 130 USD) while the other closes at 130 USD. The remaining unit
closes at 140 USD on 2024-01-01. Only FUND is selected, so sale proceeds are a
-130 USD contribution; ending value is the remaining 140 USD unit.
Profit/loss is 140 - 200 - (-130) = 70 USD. The return before the sale is
(130 + 130) / 200 - 1 = 30%; afterwards it is 140 / 130 - 1 = 7.69%.
Compounding those factors gives 40% time-weighted return. Money-weighted
return uses the actual dates of the 200 USD opening value, 130 USD withdrawal,
and 140 USD ending value. The annual rate r solves
-200 + 130 / (1 + r)^(181 / 365) + 140 / (1 + r) = 0, giving 49.65%.
The total money-weighted return is also 49.65% because the period is one year.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts '*Assets:Fund*' --commodities FUND --from 2023-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Salary
account Income:Gains
P 2022-12-31 FUND 100 USD
P 2023-07-01 FUND 130 USD
P 2024-01-01 FUND 140 USD

2022-12-31 Salary
  Assets:Cash  200 USD
  Income:Salary  -200 USD

2022-12-31 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  2 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -200 USD

2023-07-01 Partial sale
  Assets:Fund  -1 FUND {100 USD} @ 130 USD
  Assets:Cash  130 USD
  Income:Gains  -30 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 200.00 USD
Net contributions: -130.00 USD
Ending value: 140.00 USD
Profit/loss: 70.00 USD
Time-weighted return (total): 40.00 %
Time-weighted return (annualized): 40.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): 49.65 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 49.65 %

